    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754-a1">

                <pb facs="0714" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg616"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-06-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With respect to my interview with your
                    lordship on the 19th instant, in reference to my note of the 9th instant and to
                    previous correspondence, upon the subject of the detention by the British
                    authorities in South Africa of merchandise shipped by Mr. R. W. Geldart from New
                    York to Delagoa Bay, under instructions from my Government, I have the honor to
                    state that Mr. Geldart considers that $1,000 would protect him from the loss
                    with respect to the shipments on board the <hi rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi>,
                    and that he would accept that amount as full payment of his claim, and further
                    that he would accept $575 for his shipments (beer and lard) on board the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beatrice.</hi></p>
                <p>I should therefore be glad to hear your lordship’s views upon the subject and
                    whether the proposition above stated will be acceptable to Her Majesty’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
